ELASTICITY
{
Things with high ELASTICITY will be able to undergo more elastic deformation before succumbing to plastic deformation. ELASTICITY is NOT the opposite of STIFFNESS.

Elasticity is the ability of a body to resist a distorting influence and to return to its original size and shape when that influence or force is removed.
}

STIFFNESS vs COMPLIANCE
{
Stiffness is the rigidity of an object — the extent to which it resists deformation in response to an applied force.
The opposite of stiff is compliant.
}

HARDNESS VS SOFT
{
If something is hard, it will likely take a lot of effort to do something like scratch it.

PROS:
They don’t scratch as easily, and thus stay pretty longer.
They hold their edges longer.
The edges don’t deform as much on contact with other blades.
CONS: If you make something really hard, you tend to make it brittle
}

TOUGH VS BRITTLE
{
Toughness is the ability of a material to absorb energy and plastically deform without fracturing
}

weight {
 -> increased striking damage
 -> negatively affects attack speed
 -> positively affects lethality
}
hardness {
 thrust {
  -> +lethality
 }
 slash {
  -> +lethality
 }
 strike {
  -> +damage
 }
 -> ++durability
 -> ++critical failure
}
toughness {
 -> --durability
 -> --critical failure
 thrust {
  -> +damage
  -> +aim
 }
 slash {
  -> -damage
  -> ++aim
 }
 strike {
  -> +lethality
 }
}
flexibility {
 thrust {
  -> ---aim
 }
 slash {
  -> ++damage
  -> --aim
 }
}

